UPDATE Language_en_US
SET Text = 'Karakorum'
WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CITYSTATE_ZUUNMOD';

UPDATE Language_en_US
SET Text = 'Mongol'
WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CITYSTATE_ZUUNMOD_ADJ';

UPDATE Language_en_US
SET Text = 'Karakorum, founded around 1220 by Genghis Khan in central Mongolia''s Orkhon Valley, served as the capital of the Mongol Empire during its early expansion and later under Ogedei Khan, Genghis Khan''s successor. Strategically located along major trade routes, it became a cosmopolitan center of administration, commerce, and culture, attracting merchants, artisans, and diplomats from across Asia and Europe. The city housed grand palaces, temples of multiple faiths, and workshops that reflected the empire''s vast diversity and wealth. However, after Kublai Khan moved the Mongol capital to Khanbaliq (modern-day Beijing) in the late 13th century, Karakorum declined in political importance. In 1372, the Ming army under General Li Wenzhong occupied Karakorum, causing severe damage to the city. In 1380, Ming troops occupied and later razed it again. However, Karakorum was inhabited at the beginning of the 16th century, when Batumongke Dayan Khan of the Northern Yuan dynasty made it a capital once again. By the 17th century, it had largely fallen into ruins, and its remains were later used as a foundation for the construction of the Erdene Zuu Monastery, one of Mongolia''s earliest Buddhist monasteries.'
WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CITYSTATE_ZUUNMOD_PEDIA';
